<article> <header class="hero"> <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"> <a href="/">Home</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <a href="/glossary">Glossary</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <span>FATF Recommendation 16</span> </nav> <div class="hero-badge"><span class="pulse-dot"></span><span style="position:relative;z-index:1">Glossary · Schemes & Rules</span></div> <h1><span class="accent">FATF Recommendation 16</span></h1> <p class="page-meta">Glossary entry · Last reviewed 26 July 2026</p> <!-- ANSWER BLOCK — picked up by speakable schema --> <p class="answer-block"><strong>FATF Recommendation 16 (Revised)</strong> — the "Travel Rule" — sets the information that must accompany wire transfers above <strong>EUR/USD 1,000</strong>: the originator’s name and full address, and the beneficiary’s name with at minimum Town Name and Country. Industry guidance is expected end-2026, with full implementation due by end-2030.</p> </header> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">In Practice</div> <h2 class="section-title">How FATF Recommendation 16 works in practice</h2> <div class="content-block"><p>The two-stage timeline follows the SR 2026 cutover and the CPMI’s end-2027 harmonisation target, giving institutions a continuous runway. The data model behind it is identifier-neutral — LEI, BIC and national identifiers are all recognised — and in the EU the requirements are carried into law by Regulation (EU) 2023/1113.</p></div> <p class="src">Source: CPMI harmonised ISO 20022 data requirements §17 footnote / p18-6; §0.80 / R10 / p19-5; the ioNova Postal Address Specification v2.0 §10.2 (Table 22), §10.5.</p> <div class="content-block"><p>Parent reference: <a href="/address-intelligence/structured-address-mandate">ISO 20022 structured address mandate</a>.</p></div> </section> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">Citations</div> <h2 class="section-title">Sources</h2> <div class="sources-list"> <h3 class="sources-subhead">Standards &amp; regulatory sources</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://www.bis.org/cpmi/publ/d230.htm" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Harmonised ISO 20022 data requirements for enhancing cross-border payments — updated report</a> &mdash; BIS Committee on Payments and Market Infrastructures (CPMI), 26 February 2026.</li>
        <li><a href="https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2023/1113/oj" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Regulation (EU) 2023/1113 on information accompanying transfers of funds</a> &mdash; European Union, 31 May 2023.</li>
      </ul>
